course: dictionary
lesson: 9200
title: Softly, softly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Always move slowly and speak softly around small animals.» Softly here means quietly, not loudly. Speaking softly helps the animals stay calm.
explain: Softly can also mean gently, with very little force. «Snow fell softly» tells you the snow came down gently, not in a rush. Softly can even mean in a kind, tender way, like a mum closing the door softly so the baby does not wake.
explain: To find the right meaning, look at the words near softly. Words like animals, baby or asleep are clues. Then swap in quietly or gently and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Softly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done.
fact: «Softly» means quietly, not loudly.
fact: «Softly» can mean gently, with little force.
fact: «Softly» can mean in a kind, tender way.
fact: Phrases to know: «tread softly», «softly, softly», «close the door softly».
fact: In poems and music, softly can tell you how to read or play: a sad poem is often read slowly and softly.
exercise: «She spoke softly so the baby would not wake.» What does softly mean here? | *Quietly | Angrily | Hurriedly | Loudly
exercise: «Snow fell softly on the village.» What does softly tell us about the snow? | Fast and noisy | Only at night | *Gently, with little force | In a loud, angry way
exercise: Which phrase means move carefully so you make no noise? | Shout out | *Tread softly | Slam the door | Jump up
test: «Please close the door softly, the baby is asleep.» What does softly mean? | Crash it shut | Slam it hard | *Quietly and gently, so it does not wake the baby | Lock it tight
test: «She touched the puppy softly and smiled.» Which meaning fits best? | *In a kind, gentle way | Very fast | Angrily | Roughly
exam: Which word is the best swap for softly in «She spoke softly»? | Roughly | Loudly | Quickly | *Quietly
